WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.880
The women of the MCU got their due in Avengers:
Endgame, and now one of the film's directors

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:10.740
has given a spoiler-filled explanation telling
us how and why it happened.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:15.419
At the film's climax, the Avengers faced off
against a galactic army brought through a

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.380
time portal by the past version of Thanos.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:22.800
In an attempt to prevent Thanos from getting
the rebuilt Infinity Gauntlet, the team worked

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:27.040
to transport the gauntlet across the battlefield
to the quantum realm portal in Scott Lang's

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.040
van.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:32.180
And that's when a force comprised of nearly
every female hero in the Marvel Cinematic

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:36.260
Universe came together to help Captain Marvel
make the final push.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:41.160
Asked by the Los Angeles Times why he considered
it to be important for the female heroes to

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:44.740
join forces for the scene, co-director Anthony
Russo said,

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.719
Avengers: Endgame screenwriters Christopher
Markus and Stephen McFeely also opened up

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:05.120
about the all-female scene.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.060
McFeely told the New York Times

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:16.740
Markus added,

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:33.931
The scene certainly felt like a tip of the
hat to the MCU's female characters, on an

00:01:33.931 --> 00:01:38.750
even bigger scale than the team-up between
Scarlet Witch, Black Widow, and Okoye against

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:41.460
Proxima Midnight in Avengers: Infinity War.

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:45.480
But the all-female moment within Avengers:
Endgame might have hinted at even more to

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:46.420
come.

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:52.120
In late 2017, Thor: Ragnarok actress Tessa
Thompson told Comic Book Resources that she

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:56.890
and several other Marvel stars had pitched
an all-female superhero team-up film to Marvel

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:58.440
head honcho Kevin Feige.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:31.380
Feige was enthusiastic about the idea, telling
Vulture in early 2018 that it was, quote,

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:33.430
"all a matter of when and how."

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:36.170
Of course, that doesn't mean it will be any
time soon.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:40.400
Fans have been clamoring for a Black Widow
film for years, but it won't arrive until

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:45.060
2020, a whole year after the character's tragic
sacrifice in Avengers: Endgame.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:50.840
But there is precedent for an all-female team
of Avengers: in 2015, Marvel Comics unveiled

00:02:50.849 --> 00:02:55.940
A-Force, a team led by She-Hulk which included
Captain Marvel, Nico Minoru of the Runaways,

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:58.540
and Jane Foster during her stint as Thor.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:03.020
And the project may have gotten a boost from
the biggest star in the MCU, as Robert Downey

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:07.849
Jr. revealed recently on social media that
he had hosted a lunch for all of the MCU women

00:03:07.849 --> 00:03:11.100
who could attend, with some of them even coming
in character!

